# 4. CUSTOMER PROBLEM

Meridian's Strategic Account team prepares executive account briefs before important customer meetings.

Today this requires senior account managers to manually synthesize information from:

* Salesforce,
* Zendesk,
* Product Analytics,
* Google Drive,
* meeting notes,
* account history,
* stakeholder knowledge.

The obvious problem is preparation time.

But the deeper enterprise AI problem is:

> The information exists, but the judgment required to interpret it is distributed across experienced employees and is rarely written down.

Senior account managers know things such as:

* when declining usage is actually dangerous,
* when seasonality makes a decline irrelevant,
* when implementation status changes the interpretation,
* which support incidents deserve executive attention,
* whether duplicate tickets represent one issue or several,
* which meeting comments matter more than CRM fields,
* which expansion opportunities are actually credible,
* when conflicting systems should be surfaced instead of reconciled automatically.

Trace should demonstrate how this tacit expertise becomes explicit agent behavior.

